><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250630110426+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250630110428+10'00'" name="dc78a53a-2cb9-4325-a903-44a7e81c4119" page="14" coords="110.550000,457.050000,433.184000,457.050000,110.550000,443.642000,433.184000,443.642000,59.981100,444.068000,433.175000,444.068000,59.981100,430.659000,433.175000,430.659000,59.981100,431.084000,433.200000,431.084000,59.981100,417.676000,433.200000,417.676000,59.981100,418.046000,433.166000,418.046000,59.981100,404.637000,433.166000,404.637000,59.981100,405.063000,433.194000,405.063000,59.981100,391.655000,433.194000,391.655000,59.981100,392.080000,140.767000,392.080000,59.981100,378.672000,140.767000,378.672000" rect="59.562100,378.253000,433.619000,457.469000" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: Thus, if muscle fatigue is brought about by game-play and is a factor in hamstring and adductor muscle strain injuries in basketball, it does not appear to be through the fibre mechanisms investigated in this study. Based on the fibre mechanics examined in this study, the phases of increased risk for strain injury during the cut task were hypothesised as the swing-stance transition for the hamstrings and mid-late stance for the adductors.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
